    "title": "San Francisco-based company launches at-home Pap smear tool - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Danielle Ojeda ,\n39 minutes ago\nSAN FRANCISCO ( KRON ) — It’s a doctor’s appointment most women wish they could avoid. The pelvic exam, known as the pap smear, is used to detect cervical cancer-causing HPV. So, despite how uncomfortable the exam can be for some, it’s vital not to avoid your appointment.\nSan Francisco-based Teal-Health is reimagining the process for women, becoming the latest in a trend of telehealth opportunities. The current tool used in a doctor’s office for pap smears is called a speculum, and it hasn’t changed design since the 1870s. Teal Health has created a wand for women to conduct the exam on their own and meet virtually with a doctor about the results.\nDuring the latest episode of What the Health with Noelle Bellow, Teal Health Cofounder and CEO Kara Egan shows off the company’s FDA-approved sleek new wand, now available to Californians. And discusses the evolving future of healthcare.\nHow experts are using artificial intelligence to accelerate drug discoveries How to Download KRON4+ Roku: Press the Home button on your remote control, then select Streaming Channels to open the store. Next, search for KRON4+ and press add channel.\nApple TV: Open the App Store app, then search for KRON4+ and touch Get to begin downloading.\nFire TV: From the home screen, navigate to the magnifying glass icon at the top left of the screen. Search for KRON4+, select the app, and hit download to install it.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRON4.",
